BUGS REQUIRING FIXES (4 scenarios, 6 distinct bugs):
============================================================

BUG 1 - Scenarios 01: ssh_node() called with IP address
  File: chaos/scenarios/01-primary-failover/validate.sh
  Lines: 47, 83, 90
  Issue: ssh_node("54.144.241.128") fails - expects "primary" or "replica"
  Fix: Map IP back to node name, or use ssh $SSH_OPTS directly

BUG 2 - Scenarios 01, 05: Wrong column names for quant.signals INSERT
  Files: 01-primary-failover/validate.sh (lines 83-84)
         05-wal-disk-full/validate.sh (lines 74-76)
  Issue: INSERT uses (symbol, signal_type, value, generated_at) RETURNING id
  Actual: Table has (model_id, instrument_id, signal_date, score, signal_type, ...)
  Fix: Use correct columns, e.g.:
    INSERT INTO quant.signals (model_id, instrument_id, signal_date, score,
      signal_type, generated_at)
    VALUES (1, 1, CURRENT_DATE, 0.0, 'neutral', now()) RETURNING signal_id;

BUG 3 - Scenario 02: Invalid psql option --connect-timeout
  File: chaos/scenarios/02-pgbouncer-exhaustion/validate.sh
  Lines: 41, 55-56
  Issue: psql does not support --connect-timeout flag
  Fix: Use PGCONNECT_TIMEOUT=5 env var or connection string param

BUG 4 - Scenario 05: df without sudo on postgres-owned directory
  File: chaos/scenarios/05-wal-disk-full/validate.sh
  Line: 56
  Issue: df on /var/lib/pgsql/17/data/pg_wal fails without sudo (700 perms)
  Fix: ssh_primary "sudo df -BM --output=avail ${WAL_DIR} | tail -1"

BUG 5 - Scenario 07: timeout with shell function
  File: chaos/scenarios/07-slow-query-blocks-partitions/validate.sh
  Line: 88
  Issue: "timeout 8 ssh_primary" fails - timeout only works with commands, not functions
  Fix: timeout 8 ssh $SSH_OPTS ${SSH_USER}@${PRIMARY_HOST} "..."

